  "conclusion": "MODEL ESTIMATE: figures below come from an analytical model with stated assumptions, validated only where noted; they are not measurements. All 6 variants reproduce the reference on every simulated nonce, both as full pipelines (one nonce per cycle) and as iterative cores with 1 to 32 round units (mismatches: 0). Midstate pipeline: 128 stages, 1201 adders, 93696 register bits; with precompute + early reject + constant folding: 122 stages, 1062 adders (11.6% fewer), 81824 register bits (12.7% fewer). Constant folding applied to a design without midstate removes block 1 and the first three second-block rounds automatically, giving exactly the midstate + precompute datapath. ESTIMATE, not synthesized or measured: best modelled FPGA configuration midstate+precompute3+early-reject+fold on Xilinx Virtex UltraScale+ XCVU9P at up to 6.80 GH/s under the assumed clock. MEASURED for comparison: CPU 116.0 MH/s, GPU 502.1 MH/s (benchmark records bench-cpu-0002 and bench-gpu-0002). Clock, area per operator, energy per toggle and static power are assumptions; no RTL was synthesized, no timing closed, no board measured.",
